<title>USA: Allegheny Power Q1 revs down, net rises.</title>
<headline>Allegheny Power Q1 revs down, net rises.</headline>
<dateline>HAGERSTOWN, Md. 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Q1		     12 Months</p>
<p>			    1997	 1996	  1997	 1996</p>
<p>Sales to regular</p>
<p>customers,</p>
<p>  gigawatt-hours(a)  10,848     11,379	40,938     41,416</p>
<p>Revenues ($000)</p>
<p>Revenues other than</p>
<p>those related to</p>
<p>  energy		406,415    429,987   1,528,740  1,546,781</p>
<p>Energy-related</p>
<p>  revenue(b)	  208,565    218,031     765,308    798,539</p>
<p> Total		  614,980    648,018   2,294,048  2,345,320</p>
<p>Net income($000)</p>
<p>		     77,591(c)  51,418(c)  236,220(d)  214,981(d)</p>
<p>Earnings per</p>
<p>  average share     0.64(c)    0.43(c)     1.95(d)    1.79(d)</p>
<p>Average shares</p>
<p>   (000)	     121,843    120,710     121,422    120,214</p>
<p>NOTES: (a) Excludes bulk power transaction sales. (b) Primary revenues passed on to retail customers in the fuel and energy cost recovery procedures which have little effect on consolidated net income. (c) Includes restructuring charges of $39.2 million ($0.33/share) in 1996. (d) Includes restructuring charges and asset write-offs of $23.3 million ($0.19/share) in 1997 and $53.3 million ($0.45/share) in 1996.</p>
<p>Full name is Allegheny Power System Inc.</p>
<p>((--New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
